  "description": "Prognosite is an SEO and AEO intelligence platform delivered as roughly 150 callable tools, so you can investigate a site by asking questions rather than clicking through dashboards.\n\nIt starts from your own data. Connect Google Search Console and GA4 and Prognosite reads what Google and GA4 actually recorded for your properties: impressions, positions, coverage states, sessions, conversions, revenue. Most SEO connectors query a vendor's index and answer questions about the web in general. Prognosite answers questions about your site, which is what you need when the question is why a page stopped ranking last month.\n\nFirst-party data explains what happened. Explaining why usually needs more, so the platform also covers:\n\n- Site crawling. Full crawls with per-page findings, content scoring, internal link graph, sitemap and robots analysis.\n- Live SERP data. Real-time results for any keyword, feature opportunities, and comparison across Google, Bing and a privacy-focused engine.\n- Competitor and keyword research. Keyword gaps against named competitors, search volume and CPC, related and long-tail expansion, content gap recommendations.\n- Backlinks and authority. Referring domain profiles, broken inbound links worth reclaiming, and link gap comparison.\n- Performance. Lab and real-user Core Web Vitals, page speed by URL, and speed as experienced by actual visitors.\n- Bing Webmaster Tools. Crawl issues, query stats and URL submission on the Bing side.\n- Forecasting. Trend projection, seasonality detection, page lifecycle classification and what-if position modelling.\n\nThen it closes the loop. Alert rules fire on real changes rather than noise, proposed fixes become a tracked backlog, and Prognosite verifies whether each fix actually worked.\n\nEverything is mirrored in the Prognosite portal with charts, scheduled reports and audit history. Anything visible in the portal is callable by an agent, and the reverse.",
